---

<CaseStudy
  name="Dojo Tutor"
  tagline="is ClassDojo’s marketplace connecting tutors and families across a wide range of subjects, in both 1-on-1 and group formats."
  noindex
  details={[
    { label: 'Responsibilities', items: ['Product design', 'User research', 'Product building'] },
    { label: 'Collaborators', items: ['1 product manager', '4 engineers'] },
    { label: 'Platforms', items: ['Web', 'iOS and Android (launching Dec 2026)'] },
    { label: 'Years', items: ['2024–Present'] },
  ]}
>
  <Stats
    slot="meta"
    items={[
      { value: '75%+', label: 'of Dojo Tutor’s current product experience designed and shipped' },
      { value: '+12%', label: '3-month retention (relative)' },
      { value: '+20%', label: 'Lifetime value, year over year' },
    ]}
  />

  <div class="intro">
    <p>
      I own the core product experience on both sides of the marketplace, from discovery and design through
      implementation, partnering closely with engineers and often shipping features myself.
    </p>
  </div>

  <Figure images={[{ alt: 'Hero image' }]} eager />

  <div class="section-head">
    <h2>Turning Dojo Tutor into a true marketplace and growing LTV by 20% YoY</h2>
    <p>
      Dojo Tutor launched in 2023 as a matching service: the platform paired students with tutors and charged a fixed
      price for all classes. The product was an MVP, but the goal was a true marketplace where tutors could grow and run
      their own businesses.
    </p>
    <p>
      Since joining in 2024, I’ve redesigned every post-purchase surface for tutors and families. I’ve also added the
      core features a marketplace needs: schedule management, tutor-set pricing, direct messaging, automated marketing
      tools, and payment management.
    </p>
    <p>
      <span class="todo"
        >[User research: one finding or tutor/parent quote that shaped this work, e.g. what research showed families or
        tutors needed from a marketplace.]</span
      >
    </p>
  </div>

  <Figure
    images={[
      {
        alt: 'Dashboards, direct messaging, schedule management, insights, notification settings, payment history, and more',
      },
    ]}
  />

  <div class="section-head">
    <h2>Building features myself with AI coding agents</h2>
    <p>
      For these features, I used AI coding agents to build 70% of the parent-facing frontend and 80% of the
      tutor-facing frontend, with backend contributions as well.
    </p>
    <p><span class="todo">[What you built this way: one or two concrete examples.]</span></p>
    <p>
      <span class="todo"
        >[How you kept quality up: e.g. code review with engineers, tests, working inside the design system.]</span
      >
    </p>
    <p><span class="todo">[Where it broke down, and what you changed as a result.]</span></p>
  </div>

  <div class="section-head">
    <h2>Expanding from 1-on-1 tutoring to group classes and growing revenue by 10%</h2>
    <p>
      Dojo Tutor launched with 1-on-1 online tutoring only. In early 2026, we introduced group classes, our largest
      product expansion to date.
    </p>
    <p>
      I designed the tutor experience for creating and managing group classes, along with the internal tools our team
      uses to review class submissions before they reach families.
      <span class="todo"
        >[What the review guards against, e.g. inappropriate or unsafe content, misleading descriptions, low-quality
        classes, and how the tools make that review fast and consistent.]</span
      >
    </p>
    <p>Within the first 8 months of launch, group classes grew Dojo Tutor’s overall revenue by 10%.</p>
  </div>

  <Figure images={[{ alt: 'Group class form' }, { alt: 'Group class dashboard' }]} />

  <div class="section-head">
    <h2>Letting tutors set their own prices</h2>
    <p>
      Prices used to be fixed by the platform. Dojo Tutor sought to allow tutors to set their own prices, allowing them to
      charge more for specialty topics as well as open up more affordable tutoring options for families.
    </p>
    <p>
      <span class="todo"
        >[Research: what tutors were worried about, and what you learned talking to them or from data.]</span
      >
    </p>
    <p>
      I designed and built much of the frontend for tutor pricing, including the first-time experience, setting rates,
      adding discounts, and surfacing market data so tutors can price competitively.
      <span class="todo"
        >[Guardrails: how the market data and any limits kept prices fair for families and protected tutors from
        underpricing.]</span
      >
    </p>
    <p>
      <span class="todo">[Rollout: e.g. opt-in, staged release, how you communicated the change to tutors.]</span>
    </p>
    <p>Despite widespread apprehension from our tutor community, over 70% of tutors have opted into the new pricing model.</p>
  </div>

  <Figure images={[{ alt: 'Pricing onboarding' }, { alt: 'Setting prices screens' }]} />

  <div class="section-head">
    <h2>Native apps for tutors, launching December 2026</h2>
    <p>
      I designed native iOS and Android apps that let tutors message families, manage their classes, and claim open
